@startuml Germany_Lateral_Load_Rules
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontSize 13

title Germany — Lateral (Sideways) Load Overhang Rules\n(StVO §22)

start

:Load carried on vehicle;

if (Load extends laterally more than 40 cm\nbeyond outer edge of vehicle's\nparking / side lights?) then (YES — marking required)

  if (Daytime / good visibility?) then (YES)
    :Passive marking is sufficient\n(e.g. flag or reflector);
  else (NO — night or poor visibility)
    #LightYellow:**Active lighting is MANDATORY**
    Reflectors and flags alone
    are NOT sufficient at night;

    fork
      :FRONT of protruding load
      ──────────────────────
      Attach a **white light**
      facing oncoming traffic;

    fork again
      :REAR of protruding load
      ──────────────────────
      Attach a **red light**
      facing trailing traffic;

    end fork

    :Apply mounting constraints to both lights;

    note right
      **Mounting Rules:**
      ▸ Max height above road: **1.5 m**
      ▸ Position: fixed at the
        **outermost edge** of the load
        (not the car body) so other
        drivers can judge true total width
    end note

  endif

else (NO — protrusion ≤ 40 cm)
  :No special lateral marking required;
endif

#LightGreen:Lateral load marking is legally compliant;
stop

legend right
  **Key Limits at a Glance**
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lateral overhang trigger:    > 40 cm beyond
                               outer parking lights
  Night marking:               active lights only
                               (no flags/reflectors alone)
  Front light colour:          white
  Rear light colour:           red
  Max mounting height:         1.5 m above road
  Light position:              outermost edge of load
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Why it matters: standard headlights/taillights
  only show the width of the car body — a lateral
  overhang without its own lights is invisible
  to overtaking drivers, cyclists, and pedestrians.
endlegend

@enduml